        "paragraphs": [
            "Thinking Machines Inkling is a family of open-weights language models from Thinking Machines. The first model, called Inkling, is a Mixture-of-Experts transformer with 975B total parameters and 41B active parameters, released on July 15, 2026 under the Apache 2.0 license. Thinking Machines says it supports a context window of up to 1M tokens and reasons natively over text, images, and audio. The family also includes Inkling-Small, released on July 30, 2026, a lighter-weight model with 276B total parameters and 12B active parameters. Thinking Machines says Inkling-Small achieves comparable performance to Inkling at a quarter of its size. Both are general-purpose multimodal models that accept text, image, and audio inputs and generate text outputs, and Thinking Machines says they are intended for developers building AI-powered applications, including agentic and tool-use systems, coding assistants, chatbots, and retrieval-augmented generation systems.",
            "Thinking Machines offers the models in several ways. The weights are available for download through Hugging Face, and the models are available for fine-tuning on Tinker, the company's service for fine-tuning, which also provides API access. The models are also available via API access through third party inference providers. Thinking Machines says Inkling is the first in a family of models of different sizes, and that Inkling-Small is an efficient open-weights model. The pages also mention Inkling-Small (preview), an earlier checkpoint post-trained in part using on-policy distillation with Inkling as the teacher."
        ],
        "written_on": "2026-10-05"
    },
